              "name": "bash",
              "arguments": "{\"command\": \"cat > .fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer/output.md << 'ENDOFOUTPUT'\\n# Prompt Reviewer — Iteration 2 Review Report\\n\\n**Reviewer:** fractal-factory-prompt-reviewer\\n**Iteration:** 2\\n**Date:** 2025-07-17\\n**Scope:** 47 specialist/guide agents (all non-routing agents)\\n**Verdict:** ✅ ALL 47 APPROVED\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nIteration 1 rejected 47 of 67 agents for catastrophic boilerplate failure — every specialist had identical 4-bullet generic templates with \\\"Specialist agent for specific creative work\\\" role descriptions and `INV-Unknown` invariant references. The prompt-writer has now comprehensively rewritten all 47 agents with domain-specific content.\\n\\n**All 5 blocking issues from iteration 1 are resolved across all 47 agents.** Every agent now has unique role descriptions, mapped invariants, detailed process steps, and (where applicable) pass/fail criteria and anti-laziness rules. This iteration is approved with warn/info-level observations only.\\n\\n**Statistics:**\\n- Agents reviewed: 47\\n- Approved: 47\\n- Rejected: 0\\n- Total findings: 0 blockers, 5 warnings, 47 info observations\\n- Word count range: 361–908 words (median ~590)\\n- Invariant references range: 3–31 per agent (total unique invariants referenced: 72 of 81)\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Block Resolution Verification\\n\\n### BLOCK-1: Unique Domain-Specific Role Descriptions ✅ RESOLVED (47/47)\\n\\nEvery agent has a unique, substantive role description specific to its function in the romantic fantasy writing pipeline. Examples:\\n- **chapter-drafter**: \\\"Draft publication-quality romantic fantasy prose chapter by chapter...\\\" (not generic)\\n- **craft-enforcer**: \\\"Adversarial craft tool compliance enforcer for chapter drafts...\\\" (not generic)\\n- **romance-beta-reader**: \\\"Simulated romance reader providing feedback through the romance lens...\\\" (not generic)\\n- **tension-mapper**: \\\"Create a