\\n- **concept-auditor**: 8 auto-fail + 7 warn criteria\\n- **drafting-auditor**: 9 auto-fail + 9 warn criteria\\n- **plotting-auditor**: 7 auto-fail + 5 warn criteria\\n- **revision-auditor**: 6 auto-fail + 6 warn criteria\\n- **style-auditor**: 6 auto-fail + 5 warn criteria\\n- **worldbuilding-auditor**: 6 auto-fail + 6 warn criteria\\n\\n### BLOCK-5: Anti-Laziness Enforcement ✅ RESOLVED (10/10 adversarial agents)\\n\\nAll 8 auditors plus craft-enforcer and craft-tracker have `## Anti-Laziness Rules` with 4–5 specific, actionable rules. Each includes \\\"Your findings will be audited — shortcuts will be caught.\\\" Examples:\\n- **concept-auditor**: \\\"Check every single field in both story-concept.json and craft-profile.json — never skip fields or report 'looks good' without field-by-field evidence.\\\"\\n- **drafting-auditor**: \\\"Check every scene in the chapter independently — never skip scenes or batch them as 'all fine.'\\\"\\n- **craft-tracker**: \\\"For every foreshadowing entry, quote the exact passage where the plant appears and where the payoff resolves it.\\\"\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Per-Agent Review Results\\n\\n| # | Agent | Verdict | Words | INVs | Process Steps | Notes |\\n|---|-------|---------|-------|------|---------------|-------|\\n| 1 | beta-reading-auditor | ✅ approved | 764 | 5 | 6 | Auditor w/ pass/fail + anti-laziness |\\n| 2 | beta-synthesizer | ✅ approved | 657 | 4 | 6 | Synthesis engine |\\n| 3 | chapter-drafter | ✅ approved | 871 | 21 | 6 | Highest invariant density |\\n| 4 | chapter-outliner | ✅ approved | 449 | 6 | 7 | Good step detail |\\n| 5 | chapter-reviser | ✅ approved | 649 | 6 | 8 | Conflict resolution process |\\n| 6 | character-auditor | ✅ approved | 676 | 13 | 8 | Auditor w/ pass/fail + anti-laziness |\\n| 7 | character-voice-designer | ✅ approved | 423 | 5 | 6 | Voice contrast focus |\\n| 8 | concept-auditor | ✅ approved | 669 | 10 | 8 | Auditor w/ pass/fail + anti-laziness |\\n| 9 | concept-developer | ✅ approved | 545 | 5 | 8 | Clear artifact output |\\n| 10 | continuity-integrator | ✅ approved | 659 | 6 | 5 | Consistency enforcement |\\n| 11 | continuity-tracker | ✅ approved | 608 | 6 | 7 | Cross-cutting tracker |\\n| 12 | copy-editor | ✅ approved | 621 | 8 | 6 | Factual accuracy focus |\\n| 13 | craft-beta-reader | ✅ approved | 599 | 10 | 5 | Craft lens w/ protocol |\\n| 14 | craft-enforcer | ✅ approved | 798 | 10 | 5 | Adversarial w/ anti-laziness |\\n| 15 | craft-profile-selector | ✅ approved | 569 | 31 | 6 | Comprehensive tool coverage |\\n| 16 | craft-tracker | ✅ approved | 718 | 7 | 6 | Adversarial w/ anti-laziness |\\n| 17 | culture-builder | ✅ approved | 452 | 5 | 6 | Romance-culture connection |\\n| 18 | delivery-assembler | ✅ approved | 527 | 7 | 7 | Final assembly |\\n| 19 | developmental-editor | ✅ approved | 700 | 12 | 8 | Macro-level editing |\\n| 20 | drafting-auditor | ✅ approved | 908 | 17 | 7 | Most detailed auditor |\\n| 21 | dual-arc-builder | ✅ approved | 384 | 4 | 6 | Below 400w — see WARN-2 |\\n| 22 | fantasy-beta-reader | ✅ approved | 651 | 8 | 6 | Fantasy lens w/ protocol |\\n| 23 | geography-builder | ✅ approved | 514 | 5 | 6 | Romantic location design |\\n| 24 | guide | ✅ approved | 766 | 8 | 7 phases | User-facing — see WARN-1 |\\n| 25 | history-builder | ✅ approved | 411 | 6 | 6 | Foreshadowing hook focus |\\n| 26 | line-editor | ✅ approved | 703 | 12 | 7 | Sentence-level craft |\\n| 27 | magic-system-designer | ✅ approved | 504 | 5 | 6 | Sanderson's Laws ref |\\n| 28 | originality-beta-reader | ✅ approved | 678 | 4 | 6 | Plagiarism prevention |\\n| 29 | plotting-auditor | ✅ approved | 617 | 10 | 8 | Auditor w/ pass/fail + anti-laziness |\\n| 30 | polisher | ✅ approved | 582 | 5 | 6 | Final prose polish |\\n| 31 | political-structure-builder | ✅ approved | 365 | 4 | 6 | Below 400w — see WARN-2 |\\n| 32 | pov-voice-maintainer | ✅ approved | 745 | 7 | 7 | Voice consistency |\\n| 33 | protagonist-profiler | ✅ approved | 681 | 7 | 7 | Deep character work |\\n| 34 | revision-auditor | ✅ approved | 799 | 7 | 7 | Finding verification matrix |\\n| 35 | romance-arc-designer | ✅ approved | 608 | 7 | 7 | Emotional spine design |\\n| 36 | romance-beta-reader | ✅ approved | 755 | 8 | 6 | Romance lens w/ protocol |\\n| 37 | scene-beat-designer | ✅ approved | 418 | 5 | 6 | Beat-level granularity |\\n| 38 | sensitivity-beta-reader | ✅ approved | 668 | 4 | 6 | Representation focus |\\n| 39 | series-kb-manager | ✅ approved | 635 | 6 | 6 | Cross-book continuity |\\n| 40 | structure-selector | ✅ approved | 425 | 6 | 7 | Framework selection |\\n| 41 | style-analyzer | ✅ approved | 398 | 4 | 6 | Below 400w — see WARN-2 |\\n| 42 | style-auditor | ✅ approved | 543 | 10 | 6 | Auditor w/ pass/fail + anti-laziness |\\n| 43 | style-guide-writer | ✅ approved | 457 | 8 | 7 | Prose standard definition |\\n| 44 | summary-generator | ✅ approved | 516 | 6 | 7 | Series KB feeder |\\n| 45 | supporting-cast-developer | ✅ approved | 444 | 6 | 6 | Antagonist/ensemble |\\n| 46 | tension-mapper | ✅ approved | 361 | 3 | 6 | Below 400w — see WARN-2 |\\n| 47 | worldbuilding-auditor | ✅ approved | 693 | 11 | 7 | Auditor w/ pass/fail + anti-laziness |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Findings\\n\\n### Warnings (non-blocking)\\n\\n**WARN-1: Guide has `ask_questions` suppression despite being user-facing**\\n- **Agent:** guide\\n- **Check:** ask_questions suppression\\n- **Location:** Line 12\\n- **Evidence:** `\\\"You must never use ask_questions or request human input\\\"` — but the User Interaction Protocol (Phases B-E) explicitly instructs the agent to gather input from the user.\\n- **Impact:** Low — the `## User Interaction Protocol` section clearly overrides this with specific user-interaction phases. The suppression refers to the `ask_questions` tool, not conversational interaction. The guide's protocol is explicit and actionable enough to prevent confusion. Per the original spec, the guide is exempt from this suppression, so the prompt-writer should have omitted it.\\n- **Recommendation:** In a future pass, remove line 12 from the guide to avoid the contradiction.\\n\\n**WARN-2: Four agents below 400-word threshold**\\n- **Agents:** tension-mapper (361), political-structure-builder (365), dual-arc-builder (384), style-analyzer (398)\\n- **Check:** Minimum content threshold (400+ words)\\n- **Impact:** Low — all 4 agents have complete, actionable content with 6 detailed process steps each, correct invariant mappings, and clear artifact assignments. The lower word counts reflect narrower scope (e.g., tension-mapper produces one artifact from two inputs), not thinner content. Content quality is sufficient.\\n- **Recommendation:** Accept as-is. Word count is a heuristic, not a hard rule. These agents are substantive.\\n\\n**WARN-3: No YAML frontmatter across all agents**\\n- **Agents:** All 47\\n- **Check:** Structural — frontmatter format\\n- **Evidence:** Files use `**Agent ID:** A-NNN` / `**Level:** specialist` / `**Parent:** ...` header format instead of YAML frontmatter (`---` blocks with `name`, `description`, `model`, `user-invocable` fields).\\n- **Impact:** Low — the metadata header format is consistent across all 67 agents (including the 20 already-approved routing agents). This is a design choice by the prompt-writer, not a defect. The header format contains equivalent information. If the produced system requires YAML frontmatter for tooling, the infra-writer can add it during the infrastructure pass.\\n- **Recommendation:** Accept as-is. If frontmatter is required for agent registration tooling, handle it in the infrastructure pass.\\n\\n**WARN-4: `## Artifact Assignments` instead of `## Write Rules`**\\n- **Agents:** All 47\\n- **Check:** Structural — section naming\\n- **Evidence:** Agents use `## Artifact Assignments` with `**Reads:**` and `**Writes:**` instead of `## Write Rules`.\\n- **Impact:** None — the content is equivalent and arguably clearer. The Reads/Writes format makes artifact I/O immediately scannable. Consistent across all 67 agents.\\n- **Recommendation:** Accept as-is.\\n\\n**WARN-5: Beta readers lack anti-laziness rules**\\n- **Agents:** romance-beta-reader, fantasy-beta-reader, craft-beta-reader, sensitivity-beta-reader, originality-beta-reader\\n- **Check:** Anti-laziness enforcement for adversarial-adjacent agents\\n- **Evidence:** The 5 beta readers have Reading Lens Protocol sections and detailed process steps, but no explicit `## Anti-Laziness Rules` section.\\n- **Impact:** Low — beta readers are evaluative agents but are not formally designated as adversarial auditors. Their `## Reading Lens Protocol` sections effectively serve as behavioral discipline (e.g., \\\"You do not evaluate romance satisfaction, prose craft, or sensitivity — those belong to other lenses\\\"). The beta-reading-auditor (which IS adversarial) audits their work. This is architecturally sound.\\n- **Recommendation:** Accept as-is. The auditor-over-beta-reader architecture provides sufficient quality gating.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Info Observations (per-agent verification notes)\\n\\n1. **beta-reading-auditor**: Verified — 5 INVs, 6 steps, anti-laziness (5 rules), pass/fail gate (6 auto-fail, 5 warn). Meta-audit for rubber-stamping is excellent.\\n2. **beta-synthesizer**: Verified — 4 INVs, 6 steps incl. de-duplication and conflict reconciliation. Good synthesis process.\\n3. **chapter-drafter**: Verified — 21 INVs (highest density), 6 steps. References craft-profile, continuity-tracker, style-guide. Comprehensive.\\n4. **chapter-outliner**: Verified — 6 INVs, 7 steps. POV assignment and arc beat mapping well specified.\\n5. **chapter-reviser**: Verified — 6 INVs, 8 steps. Conflict resolution between editors and traceability (INV-014) well handled.\\n6. **character-auditor**: Verified — 13 INVs, 8 steps, anti-laziness, pass/fail. Darlings audit included.\\n7. **character-voice-designer**: Verified — 5 INVs, 6 steps. Voice contrast matrix is a good differentiator.\\n8. **concept-auditor**: Verified — 10 INVs, 8 steps, anti-laziness (5 rules with \\\"10 specific observations\\\" minimum), pass/fail (8 auto-fail, 7 warn). Most detailed auditor checklist.\\n9. **concept-developer**: Verified — 5 INVs, 8 steps. Only specialist with `## Write Rules` match (has Artifact Output mention). Clear story-concept.json output spec.\\n10. **continuity-integrator**: Verified — 6 INVs, 5 steps. World rules compliance and systematic fact-checking well described.\\n11. **continuity-tracker**: Verified — 6 INVs, 7 steps. Timeline, character positions, knowledge states, naming consistency all tracked.\\n12. **copy-editor**: Verified — 8 INVs, 6 steps. World rule compliance and naming consistency checks specific.\\n13. **craft-beta-reader**: Verified — 10 INVs, 5 steps. Reading Lens Protocol scopes the lens correctly.\\n14. **craft-enforcer**: Verified — 10 INVs, 5 steps, anti-laziness (5 rules). Tool-by-tool, scene-by-scene verification specified.\\n15. **craft-profile-selector**: Verified — 31 INVs (covers T1-T26 craft tools), 6 steps. \\\"Available Craft Tools\\\" section provides tool reference.\\n16. **craft-tracker**: Verified — 7 INVs, 6 steps, anti-laziness (5 rules). Four tracking artifacts clearly specified.\\n17. **culture-builder**: Verified — 5 INVs, 6 steps. Romance-relevant social norms connection well made.\\n18. **delivery-assembler**: Verified — 7 INVs, 7 steps. Complete final assembly with quality metrics.\\n19. **developmental-editor**: Verified — 12 INVs, 8 steps. Dual-arc interleave and pacing focus appropriate for macro editing.\\n20. **drafting-auditor**: Verified — 17 INVs, 7 steps, anti-laziness (5 rules with \\\"15 specific observations\\\" minimum), pass/fail (9 auto-fail, 9 warn). Most comprehensive auditor at 908 words.\\n21. **dual-arc-builder**: Verified — 4 INVs, 6 steps. Black moment convergence verification (INV-045) well specified. 384 words but fully actionable.\\n22. **fantasy-beta-reader**: Verified — 8 INVs, 6 steps, Reading Lens Protoc