        "reasoning_text": "Now I can see the actual agent file structure. The files DON'T use YAML frontmatter with `---` delimiters like typical .agent.md files. Instead they use a different format with:\n\n- H1 heading (display name)\n- Metadata lines like `**Agent ID:**`, `**Level:**`, `**Parent:**`, `**Children:**`, `**Pass/Phase:**`\n- `## Role` section (instead of a simple role description paragraph before first H2)\n- `## Key Invariants` section\n- `## Process` section with numbered steps (for specialists)\n- `## Pure Router Purity Rule` section (for coordinators/orchestrators)\n\n\n- `## Routing Table` section with pipe-delimited table (for coordinators/orchestrators)\n- `## Artifact Assignments` with Reads/Writes\n- `## Result Codes` section\n- `## Status Contract` section\n- Anti-laziness auditors have `## Anti-Laziness Rules` section\n\nSo my validation script needs to be adapted to match this actual format rather than assuming YAML frontmatter. The frontmatter checks need to look for the `**Agent ID:**` style metadata instead, and I need to update the section validation logic to account for all these different section types.\n\nLooking at the beta-synthesizer file, it actually has solid content across all sections—the real problem was my parser expecting YAML frontmatter that isn't there. I need to rewrite the validation script to properly handle the actual file structure.",
        "role": "assistant",
