              "name": "create",
              "arguments": "{\"file_text\": \"# Coverage Hunter — Cycle 1 Report\\n\\n**Agent:** fractal-factory-coverage-hunter\\n**Cycle:** 1\\n**Domain:** fantasy-writer (romantic-fantasy-writer)\\n**Date:** 2026-03-16\\n\\n## Executive Summary\\n\\nSearched 3 categories across the produced 67-agent romantic fantasy writer system. Found **4 gaps (3 critical, 1 warning)** across 2 categories. Subdomain coverage is clean.\\n\\n| Category | Status | Gaps |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 1. Subdomain Coverage | ✅ CLEAN | 0 |\\n| 2. Invariant Enforcement | ❌ DIRTY | 2 (1 critical, 1 warning) |\\n| 3. Routing Completeness | ❌ DIRTY | 2 (2 critical) |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 1: Subdomain Coverage\\n\\n**Status:** CLEAN\\n**Methodology:** For each of 14 subdomains, verified (a) at least one specialist agent is responsible via roster 'pass' field, (b) prompt file exists in produced output, (c) test scenarios exercise the subdomain via relatedInvariants→affectedSubdomains mapping.\\n\\n### Coverage Matrix\\n\\n| Subdomain | Agent Count | Pass | Test Scenarios | Status |\\n|---|---|---|---|---|\\n| SD-001 user-guide-and-input | 1 | guide | 4 | ✅ |\\n| SD-002 concept-development | 4 | concept | 4 | ✅ |\\n| SD-003 worldbuilding | 9 | worldbuilding | 11 | ✅ |\\n| SD-004 character-development | 8 | character | 9 | ✅ |\\n| SD-005 plotting-and-outlining | 9 | plotting | 8 | ✅ |\\n| SD-006 prose-style-calibration | 4 | style | 9 | ✅ |\\n| SD-007 chapter-drafting | 8 | drafting | 21 | ✅ |\\n| SD-008 revision-and-editing | 6 | revision | 21 | ✅ |\\n| SD-009 beta-reading-simulation | 10 | beta-reading | 20 | ✅ |\\n| SD-010 polish-and-delivery | 4 | polish | 4 | ✅ |\\n| SD-011 adversarial-consistency | 8 | cross-phase auditors | 11 | ✅ |\\n| SD-012 series-knowledge-management | 2 | cross-cutting | 11 | ✅ |\\n| SD-013 continuity-tracking | 2 | cross-cutting/drafting | 11 | ✅ |\\n| SD-014 craft-knowledge-systems | 3 | cross-cutting/concept | 5 | ✅ |\\n\\n**Conclusion:** All 14 subdomains are covered by at least one agent with dedicated prompt files and test scenarios. No gaps found.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 2: Invariant Enforcement\\n\\n**Status:** DIRTY (1 critical, 1 warning)\\n**Methodology:** Searched all 67 agent prompts for explicit INV-NNN references via regex. For invariants with ≤1 reference, performed secondary keyword search. Verified craft-tool invariants (INV-039–064) are handled by dynamic craft-profile mechanism. 80 of 81 invariants are referenced by at least one agent prompt.\\n\\n### Gap IE-001: INV-030 (No Silent Failures) — CRITICAL\\n\\n**Invariant:** \\\"If an agent cannot complete its task, it MUST surface the problem explicitly rather than producing low-quality output.\\\"\\n\\n**Classification:** behavioral | **Affected subdomains:** ALL 14\\n\\n**Finding:** INV-030 is not referenced by any of the 67 produced agent prompts. Zero matches for:\\n- `INV-030` (regex across all files)\\n- `silent fail` / `surface problem` / `explicit failure` (natural language search)\\n\\nThis is a universal safety invariant. Without it, agents may silently degrade output quality — producing mediocre prose, incomplete worldbuilding, or superficial revisions — without flagging the issue. The `blocked` result code exists but no agent is instructed to prefer it over low-quality output.\\n\\n**Impact:** High. A chapter drafter that struggles with a scene might produce bland filler rather than reporting the difficulty. An auditor might wave through marginal work rather than acknowledging it can't properly evaluate something.\\n\\n**Suggested Fix:** Add INV-030 to the Key Invariants section of:\\n- All 8 auditor agents (mandatory — they are the last line of defense)\\n- All 9 coordinators (they should escalate rather than accept silent degradation)\\n- All creative specialists (chapter-drafter, line-editor, etc.)\\n- The orchestrator itself\\n\\n**Re-entry target:** execution (prompt rewriting)\\n\\n### Gap IE-002: INV-063 (Thematic Argument Scaffolding / T25) — WARNING\\n\\n**Invariant:** \\\"Structure each theme as an argument — question, competing answers (embodied by characters/factions), resolution earned through protagonist experience.\\\"\\n\\n**Classification:** quality craft tool | **Affected subdomains:** SD-002, SD-005, SD-011\\n\\n**Finding:** Only referenced by craft-profile-selector (1 agent). When T25 is selected as an active craft tool:\\n- **Craft-enforcer:** Process steps enumerate T1, T2, T3, T14, T15, T16, T19, T20, T22, T23 — but NOT T25. Step 1 says \\\"build a checklist for each active tool\\\" but Steps 3-4 only provide instructions for 10 of 26 tools.\\n- **Concept-auditor:** Loads craft-profile.json dynamically but has no T25-specific verification logic.\\n- **Plotting-auditor:** Same — no T25-specific checking.\\n\\n**Impact:** Medium. If T25 is selected, no agent has explicit instructions on HOW to verify thematic argument scaffolding. The dynamic craft-profile loading mechanism exists but relies on the agent improvising verification without guidance.\\n\\n**Suggested Fix:** Add T25 verification instructions to:\\n- Craft-enforcer's chapter-level audit (Step 4): \\\"T25 (Thematic Argument): Verify thematic question raised in opening chapters, competing answers embodied by characters, resolution earned through experience.\\\"\\n- Concept-auditor's process: verify thematic argument documented in concept artifacts.\\n- Expand craft-enforcer to cover all 26 tools, not just the 10 currently enumerated.\\n\\n**Re-entry target:** execution (prompt rewriting)\\n\\n### Invariant Coverage Statistics\\n\\n| Coverage Level | Count | Percentage |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| 3+ agents enforce | 69 | 85.2% |\\n| 2 agents enforce | 6 | 7.4% |\\n| 1 agent enforces | 5 | 6.2% |\\n| 0 agents enforce | 1 | 1.2% |\\n| **Total** | **81** | **100%** |\\n\\nSingle-agent invariants (potential fragility): INV-025 (originality-beta-reader only), INV-028 (style-analyzer only), INV-065 (guide only), INV-067 (guide only), INV-077 (guide only). These are acceptable because they are specialized to a single agent's domain.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 3: Routing Completeness\\n\\n**Status:** DIRTY (2 critical)\\n**Methodology:** Traced every execution path through the orchestrator's 24 routing entries and all 20 coordinator/sub-coordinator routing tables. Verified every child agent's result codes have handlers in their parent. Checked convergence bounds. Verified cross-cutting agent routing.\\n\\n### Items Verified\\n\\n- **Orchestrator:** 24 routes, 12 dispatch targets, 3 terminal result codes (delivered, delivered-with-gaps, failed)\\n- **9 Coordinators:** All have complete/blocked/revision-loop result code handling\\n- **10 Sub-coordinators:** All have complete/blocked result code handling\\n- **Revision-beta outer loop:** Bounded (maxCycles: 2) with fallback action ✅\\n- **Auditor retry loops:** All bounded (maxRetries: 3) with escalate-blocked ✅\\n- **revision-loop transient state:** Wildcard handler in orchestrator ✅\\n- **Cross-cutting agents:** ❌ INCOMPLETE\\n\\n### Gap RC-001: craft-tracker 'blocked' Unhandled — CRITICAL\\n\\n**Finding:** The orchestrator routing table has only ONE route for craft-tracker:\\n```\\nread=agents/craft-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'completed' AND phaseStatuses.drafting.status == 'pending'\\naction: dispatch romantic-fantasy-writer-drafting-coordinator\\n```\\n\\nThe craft-tracker agent prompt defines TWO result codes:\\n- `completed` — all tracking artifacts updated ✅ handled\\n- `blocked` — craft-profile.json missing or chapter content unavailable ❌ NO HANDLER\\n\\n**Impact:** If craft-tracker fails (e.g., craft-profile.json wasn't created by concept phase), the orchestrator has no matching route. The pipeline stalls indefinitely — no error reporting, no fallback, no recovery.\\n\\n**Suggested Fix:** Add route to orchestrator:\\n```\\nread=agents/craft-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'blocked'\\naction: write own status: failed; summary: 'Craft tracking initialization failed — craft-profile.json may be missing'\\n```\\n\\n**Re-entry target:** execution (orchestrator prompt + routing.json)\\n\\n### Gap RC-002: continuity-tracker 'blocked' Unhandled — CRITICAL\\n\\n**Finding:** The orchestrator routing table has only ONE route for continuity-tracker:\\n```\\nread=agents/continuity-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'completed' AND phaseStatuses.revision.status == 'pending'\\naction: dispatch romantic-fantasy-writer-revision-coordinator\\n```\\n\\nThe continuity-tracker agent prompt defines TWO result codes:\\n- `completed` — continuity tracker updated ✅ handled\\n- `blocked` — chapter content unavailable or world-bible files missing ❌ NO HANDLER\\n\\n**Impact:** If continuity-tracker fails (e.g., world-bible files corrupted or missing), the orchestrator stalls. Same pattern as RC-001.\\n\\n**Suggested Fix:** Add route to orchestrator:\\n```\\nread=agents/continuity-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'blocked'\\naction: write own status: failed; summary: 'Continuity verification failed — required artifacts missing'\\n```\\n\\n**Re-entry target:** execution (orchestrator prompt + routing.json)\\n\\n### Routing Health Summary\\n\\n| Agent Level | Total Routes | Handlers Complete | Gaps |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| Orchestrator | 24 | 22 of 24 needed | 2 missing |\\n| Coordinators (9) | 89 | 89 of 89 | 0 |\\n| Sub-coordinators (10) | 50 | 50 of 50 | 0 |\\n| **Total** | **163** | **161** | **2** |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Second-Pass Verification\\n\\nPer anti-laziness rules, I performed a second pass with different search strategies:\\n\\n1. **Subdomain coverage second pass:** Instead of relying on pass-field mapping, I checked each subdomain's invariants and verified the agents referenced by those invariants exist. All subdomains confirmed covered.\\n\\n2. **Invariant enforcement second pass:** Searched for natural-language synonyms of each invariant (e.g., \\\"silent\\\" for INV-030, \\\"subtext\\\" for INV-062, \\\"thematic\\\" for INV-063). Found line-editor handles INV-062 (subtext gap) via keyword match even though it doesn't cite the INV ID. Confirmed INV-030 has zero behavioral coverage.\\n\\n3. **Routing completeness second pass:** Checked all per-chapter coordinator routing for initial dispatch conditions, chapter iteration, and termination. All 3 per-chapter coordinators (drafting, revision, beta-reading) have complete routing with proper initialization, iteration, and termination conditions.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Recommendations for Cycle 2\\n\\nIf gaps are addressed and cycle 2 runs:\\n1. Verify INV-030 has been added to agent prompts\\n2. Verify orchestrator routing table has craft-tracker and continuity-tracker blocked handlers\\n3. Verify craft-enforcer process steps cover T25\\n\\n**Overall verdict: DIRTY — 4 gaps found (3 critical, 1 warning). Re-entry to execution pass recommended.**\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-coverage-hunter/output.md\"}"
            }
