cter/gate.json; delete sub-coordinator + specialist + auditor statuses; increment retries; re-dispatch'. No test scenario exercises this.\\\",\\n          \\\"reEntryTarget\\\": \\\"planning\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"TC-005\\\",\\n          \\\"severity\\\": \\\"warning\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"No test covers series/sequel production. The system includes series-kb-manager (reads all world-bible, characters, chapter-summaries) and story-config.json has sequelOf/seriesId fields. The architecture explicitly designs for series production ('series production from day one') but no scenario tests sequel creation where a previous book's series-kb influences worldbuilding, character, or plot decisions.\\\",\\n          \\\"affectedFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/test-plan.json\\\"],\\n          \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"story-config.json schema: sequelOf (string|null), seriesId (string|null). series-kb-manager reads all major artifacts. No test scenario contains 'series' or 'sequel' in description/trigger/expected fields.\\\",\\n          \\\"reEntryTarget\\\": \\\"planning\\\"\\n        },\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"TC-006\\\",\\n          \\\"severity\\\": \\\"warning\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"No test specifically exercises parallel agent dispatch (beta-reader fan-out). The beta-reading phase uses two parallel groups: genre-lens-coordinator dispatches romance + fantasy beta-readers in parallel, craft-lens-coordinator dispatches craft + sensitivity + originality beta-readers in parallel. No test verifies parallel dispatch, fan-out/fan-in synchronization, or partial failure within a parallel group.\\\",\\n          \\\"affectedFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/test-plan.json\\\"],\\n          \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"routing.json genre-lens-coordinator.parallelGroups: ['romance-beta-reader', 'fantasy-beta-reader']. routing.json craft-lens-coordinator.parallelGroups: ['craft-beta-reader', 'sensitivity-beta-reader', 'originality-beta-reader']. No test scenario contains 'parallel' in any field.\\\",\\n          \\\"reEntryTarget\\\": \\\"planning\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": 6,\\n      \\\"name\\\": \\\"Cross-Reference Integrity\\\",\\n      \\\"status\\\": \\\"dirty\\\",\\n      \\\"methodology\\\": \\\"Verified 6 cross-reference dimensions: (1) All agent names in routing.json dispatchOrder, routingTable actions, and parallelGroups resolve to roster.json entries — extracted names via regex pattern matching. (2) All 67 roster agents have corresponding .agent.md prompt files in produced-output/agents/. (3) No orphan prompt files exist without roster entries. (4) All coordinators/orchestrator/sub-coordinators in roster have entries in routing.json. (5) All result codes referenced in routing table conditions match the target agent's resultCodes in roster. (6) Roster parent/children references are bidirectionally consistent. (7) Architecture.json artifact writer/reader names resolve to roster agent names.\\\",\\n      \\\"itemsChecked\\\": 67,\\n      \\\"gapsFound\\\": 1,\\n      \\\"gaps\\\": [\\n        {\\n          \\\"id\\\": \\\"CR-001\\\",\\n          \\\"severity\\\": \\\"warning\\\",\\n          \\\"description\\\": \\\"architecture.json contains 6 ghost agent names in artifact writer/reader fields that do not exist in roster.json. These are pre-depth-analysis collapsed role names that were never updated after the depth analyzer split them into specialists: (1) 'romantic-fantasy-writer-orchestrator' → should be 'romantic-fantasy-writer' (appears in progress.json and manifest.json metadata). (2) 'romantic-fantasy-writer-worldbuilder' → split into 5 specialists (appears in 5 world-bible artifact writers). (3) 'romantic-fantasy-writer-character-developer' → split into 4 specialists (appears in characters and romance-arc writers). (4) 'romantic-fantasy-writer-plot-architect' → split into 5 specialists (appears in craft-profile, plot-structure, dual-arc, chapter-outlines, tension-map writers). (5) 'romantic-fantasy-writer-style-calibrator' → renamed to style-guide-writer (appears in style-guide writer). (6) 'romantic-fantasy-writer-adversarial-auditor' → split into 7 per-phase auditors (appears in audit-reports writer). Impact: architecture.json artifact metadata is unreliable for determining which agent actually writes/reads which artifact. The routing.json and roster.json are internally consistent and correct.\\\",\\n          \\\"affectedFiles\\\": [\\\".fractal-factory/architecture.json\\\"],\\n          \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"6 ghost names with 0 matches in roster.json's 67 agents. Routing.json agent references: all resolve ✓. Roster parent/child: all resolve ✓. Prompt files: 67/67 present ✓. Result codes: all valid ✓.\\\",\\n          \\\"reEntryTarget\\\": \\\"planning\\\"\\n        }\\n      ]\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"summary\\\": {\\n    \\\"totalCategories\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"categoriesClean\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"categoriesDirty\\\": 3,\\n    \\\"totalGaps\\\": 10,\\n    \\\"criticalGaps\\\": 0,\\n    \\\"warningGaps\\\": 10,\\n    \\\"narrative\\\": \\\"Cycle 1 artifact hunt found 10 warning-level gaps across all 3 categories, zero critical. Category 4 (Artifact Coverage): All 42 artifacts have schema documentation and at least one real writer/reader in the roster, but architecture.json has stale writer metadata — 6 ghost agent names from pre-depth-analysis design, and one writer attribution error (chapter-summaries). The craft-profile multi-writer protocol referencing a phantom plot-architect agent is unimplementable as designed. Category 5 (Test Coverage): 21 scenarios cover most paths but miss the delivered-with-gaps result code, plotting/character auditor rejections, series/sequel production, and parallel dispatch. 3 golden test fixtures are missing. Category 6 (Cross-Reference Integrity): The routing.json ↔ roster.json ↔ prompt-files triangle is fully consistent — all agent names, result codes, parent/child, and dispatch orders resolve. The only cross-reference issue is the architecture.json ghost names, which are documentation drift that doesn't affect runtime.\\\"\\n  }\\n}\\n\"}"
