t scenarios from `test-plan.json` are missing from the `tests/` directory:\\n- **TEST-014**: \\\"Edge case: no style references\\\" — style-coordinator handles absent reference texts\\n- **TEST-016**: \\\"Specialist: geography-builder creates map\\\" — geography-builder produces valid artifact\\n- **TEST-017**: \\\"Specialist: romance-arc-designer dual arc\\\" — romance-arc-designer creates dual protagonist arc\\n\\nThe plan specifies 21 scenarios but only 18 were produced (85.7% coverage).\\n\\n**DC-W03** (warning): README.md mentions \\\"blocked\\\" only once and provides no recovery guidance. Missing: how to diagnose blocked states, how to resume after failure, whether manual intervention is possible, how to reset a phase. The README lacks any \\\"Error Handling\\\", \\\"Troubleshooting\\\", or \\\"Recovery\\\" section. A user encountering a failed or blocked pipeline would have no documented path forward.\\n\\n**DC-W04** (warning): `profile.json` has no `skills` section despite 9 skill directories existing in `skills/`. Without a skills section in the deployment config, skills would not be automatically mounted into agent containers. The skills directory is functionally disconnected from the deployment pipeline.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Category 9: Meta-Knowledge Infrastructure\\n\\n**Status**: dirty (3 warnings)\\n\\n### Methodology\\n\\n1. Inspected all 9 skill files in `skills/` (18–29 lines each) for domain relevance\\n2. Searched all 67 `.agent.md` files for skill references using regex patterns: `skills/`, `SKILL`, `invoke.*skill`, `use.*skill`\\n3. Checked `profile.json` for skills configuration\\n4. Assessed whether each skill's content is specific to the romantic fantasy writing domain\\n5. Verified whether skill stubs reference external sources that exist within the produced system\\n\\n### Items Checked: 85\\n\\n| Check | Count | Result |\\n|-------|-------|--------|\\n| Skill files inspected | 9 | ⚠️ All infrastructure, zero domain-specific |\\n| Agent prompts searched for skill refs | 67 | ⚠️ Zero references found |\\n| Profile.json skills config | 1 | ⚠️ Section missing |\\n| Skill self-containedness | 9 | ⚠️ 3+ reference external sources |\\n\\n### Gaps\\n\\n**MK-W01** (warning): All 9 skills are infrastructure/template stubs — none are domain-specific. The skills are: `agent-as-function-contract`, `dockerfile-pattern`, `fractal-coordinator-patterns`, `fractal-orchestrator-architecture`, `mcp-sidecar`, `profile-config`, `prompt-security`, `rules`, `web-fetch`. The system has no skills for: the 26 craft tools (T1–T26), genre conventions, romantic fantasy tropes, creative writing techniques, or any of the 81 invariants. All domain knowledge is embedded directly in agent prompts rather than being reusable skill artifacts.\\n\\n**MK-W02** (warning): Zero agent prompt files reference any skill from the `skills/` directory. The only match for \\\"skill\\\" across all 67 agents was in `magic-system-designer.agent.md`, which uses the word in domain context (\\\"learned skill\\\" referring to how magic is accessed), not as a system skill reference. The skills directory is entirely disconnected from the agent system — no agent reads, invokes, or is wired to any skill.\\n\\n**MK-W03** (warning): Infrastructure skill stubs reference external \\\"Ralph Orchestrator\\\" sources that don't exist within the produced system. Example: `rules/SKILL.md` says *\\\"See the Ralph Orchestrator's standard rules skill for the canonical list.\\\"* These dangling references make skills non-self-contained. A user deploying the romantic-fantasy-writer as a standalone system would find stub skills pointing to nonexistent external documents.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\n| Category | Status | Gaps | Critical | Warning |\\n|----------|--------|------|----------|---------|\\n| 7. Bootstrap Completeness | clean | 1 | 0 | 1 |\\n| 8. Documentation Completeness | dirty | 4 | 0 | 4 |\\n| 9. Meta-Knowledge Infrastructure | dirty | 3 | 0 | 3 |\\n| **Total** | **dirty** | **8** | **0** | **8** |\\n\\n### Key Themes\\n\\n1. **Bootstrap is solid**: Perfect agent coverage (67/67), all directories and seeds in place. Only a minor naming inconsistency between architecture.json and actual series-kb path.\\n\\n2. **Documentation has gaps for operational readiness**: The README is comprehensive for understanding the system's architecture, but lacks operational documentation (test suite, error recovery, troubleshooting) that a user would need when actually running the pipeline.\\n\\n3. **Skills are disconnected infrastructure stubs**: The 9 skills appear to be template copies from the Fractal Factory exemplar system. They serve no purpose in the produced romantic-fantasy-writer — no agent references them, profile.json doesn't wire them, and none contain domain-specific knowledge. The entire skills layer needs either: (a) being removed if skills aren't part of the agent system's architecture, or (b) being replaced with domain-specific skills and properly wired into agent prompts and profile.json.\\n\\n### Re-entry Recommendation\\n\\nAll 8 gaps have `reEntryTarget: execution` — they require prompt-writer and infra-writer updates, not architectural changes. No re-entry to planning or analysis is needed.\\n\", \"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-infrastructure-hunter/output.md\"}"
