ts that define 'blocked' have corresponding handler routes in their parent's routing table. No additional changes needed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ],\\n  \\\"gapsNotRequiringRoutingChanges\\\": [\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AC-002\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"craft-profile.json single-writer change is an architecture/roster concern. Routing already dispatches craft-profile-selector only from concept-coordinator — no routing change needed.\\\"\\n    },\\n    {\\n      \\\"id\\\": \\\"IE-002\\\",\\n      \\\"note\\\": \\\"T25 thematic argument scaffolding enforcement is a prompt-level concern for auditor agents, not a routing concern. No routing change needed.\\\"\\n    }\\n  ]\\n}\\n\"}"
