              "arguments": "{\"path\": \"/home/jakubs/repositories/ralph-orchestrator/.fractal-factory/agents/fractal-factory-routing-planner/output.md\", \"file_text\": \"# Routing Planner Output — Re-Entry Cycle 2\\n\\n## Summary\\n\\nRe-entry execution triggered by gap-hunting pass (cycle 1 → 2). Fixed 2 critical routing gaps and performed a full completeness audit across all 20 routed agents.\\n\\n**Changes made**: 2 new routes added to orchestrator routing table\\n**Routes audited**: 160 total (26 orchestrator + 134 across 19 coordinators)\\n**Unhandled result codes remaining**: 0\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Critical Gaps Fixed\\n\\n### RC-001: craft-tracker blocked handler (CRITICAL → FIXED)\\n\\n**Problem**: The orchestrator routing table had only one route for craft-tracker:\\n```\\nread: agents/craft-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'completed' AND phaseStatuses.drafting.status == 'pending'\\naction: dispatch drafting-coordinator\\n```\\nIf craft-tracker returned `blocked` (craft-profile.json missing or chapter content unavailable), no route matched and the pipeline would stall indefinitely.\\n\\n**Fix**: Added new route after the existing craft-tracker completion route:\\n```\\nread: agents/craft-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'blocked'\\naction: write own status: failed; summary: 'Craft tracking initialization failed — craft-profile.json missing or chapter content unavailable'\\n```\\n\\nThis follows the established pattern used by all 9 coordinator blocked handlers — mandatory phases report `failed` to the orchestrator.\\n\\n### RC-002: continuity-tracker blocked handler (CRITICAL → FIXED)\\n\\n**Problem**: The orchestrator routing table had only one route for continuity-tracker:\\n```\\nread: agents/continuity-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'completed' AND phaseStatuses.revision.status == 'pending'\\naction: dispatch revision-coordinator\\n```\\nIf continuity-tracker returned `blocked` (chapter content unavailable or world-bible files missing), no route matched and the pipeline would stall indefinitely.\\n\\n**Fix**: Added new route after the existing continuity-tracker completion route:\\n```\\nread: agents/continuity-tracker/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'blocked'\\naction: write own status: failed; summary: 'Continuity verification failed — chapter content unavailable or world-bible files missing'\\n```\\n\\n---\\n\\n## IE-001 Audit: Blocked Handler Completeness\\n\\nAudited all routing tables in response to IE-001 (INV-030: No Silent Failures). Results:\\n\\n### Orchestrator — Direct Children (12 agents)\\n\\nAll 12 direct children of the orchestrator now have both completion and blocked handlers:\\n\\n| Child | Completion Handler | Blocked Handler |\\n|-------|-------------------|-----------------|\\n| concept-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to worldbuilding | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| worldbuilding-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to character | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| character-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to plotting | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| plotting-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to style | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| style-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to craft-tracker | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| craft-tracker | ✅ `completed` → dispatch drafting | ✅ `blocked` → fail **(NEW)** |\\n| drafting-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to continuity-tracker | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| continuity-tracker | ✅ `completed` → dispatch revision | ✅ `blocked` → fail **(NEW)** |\\n| revision-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to beta-reading | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| beta-reading-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → check loop / advance | ✅ `blocked` → fail |\\n| polish-coordinator | ✅ `complete` → advance to series-kb | ✅ `blocked` → delivered-with-gaps |\\n| series-kb-manager | ✅ `completed` → delivered | ✅ `blocked` → delivered-with-gaps |\\n\\nAdditionally, the wildcard handler covers all coordinators' transient `revision-loop` state:\\n```\\nread: agents/{any-coordinator}/status.json\\ncondition: result == 'revision-loop'\\naction: Wait — re-read on next routing cycle\\n```\\n\\n### Coordinators — Loop Config Auditor Coverage (8 loops)\\n\\nAll 8 coordinators with writer→auditor loops handle all 3 auditor result codes:\\n\\n| Coordinator | Auditor | `passed` | `failed` (retry) | `failed` (max) | `blocked` |\\n|-------------|---------|----------|-------------------|-----------------|-----------|\\n| concept-coordinator | concept-auditor | ✅ complete | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| worldbuilding-coordinator | worldbuilding-auditor | ✅ complete | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| character-coordinator | character-auditor | ✅ complete | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| plotting-coordinator | plotting-auditor | ✅ complete | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| style-coordinator | style-auditor | ✅ complete | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| drafting-coordinator | drafting-auditor | ✅ advance ch. | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| revision-coordinator | revision-auditor | ✅ advance ch. | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n| beta-reading-coordinator | beta-reading-auditor | ✅ advance ch. | ✅ re-dispatch | ✅ blocked | ✅ blocked |\\n\\n### Sub-Coordinators — Sequential Child Coverage (10 sub-coordinators)\\n\\nAll 10 sub-coordinators handle both `completed`/`complete` and `blocked` for every child:\\n\\n| Sub-Coordinator | Children | All Completion Handlers | All Blocked Handlers |\\n|-----------------|----------|------------------------|---------------------|\\n| physical-world-coordinator | 3 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| systems-world-coordinator | 2 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| core-characters-coordinator | 2 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| ensemble-coordinator | 2 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| structural-design-coordinator | 3 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| chapter-design-coordinator | 2 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| creative-writing-coordinator | 2 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| quality-integration-coordinator | 2 specialists | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| genre-lens-coordinator | 2 specialists (parallel) | ✅ | ✅ |\\n| craft-lens-coordinator | 3 specialists (parallel) | ✅ | ✅ |\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Gaps Not Requiring Routing Changes\\n\\n### AC-002: craft-profile.json single-writer protocol\\nThe roster planner updated architecture.json so craft-profile.json is now single-writer (craft-profile-selector, create-once). Routing already dispatches craft-profile-selector only through concept-coordinator, so no routing change is needed.\\n\\n### IE-002: INV-063 / Craft Tool T25 coverage\\nT25 thematic argument scaffolding enforcement is a prompt-level concern for auditor agents. It does not affect routing — auditors already gate on all craft tools via their auditing checklist. No routing change needed.\\n\\n---\\n\\n## Routing Architecture Summary\\n\\n### Pipeline Flow (orchestrator)\\n```\\nconcept → worldbuilding → character → plotting → style → craft-tracker →\\n  drafting → continuity-tracker → revision → beta-reading → polish → series-kb\\n```\\n\\nWith revision↔beta-reading loop (max 2 cycles) and mandatory phase failure propagation.\\n\\n### Convergence Bounds\\n- **Auditor retry loops**: max 3 retries (globalBounds.maxAuditorRetries)\\n- **Revision↔beta-reading cycles**: max 2 (globalBounds.maxRevisionBetaCycles)\\n- **Chapter checkpoint interval**: every 5 chapters (globalBounds.maxChaptersBeforeCheckpoint)\\n\\n### Result Code Taxonomy\\n- **Orchestrator**: `delivered` | `delivered-with-gaps` | `failed`\\n- **Coordinators**: `complete` | `blocked` | `revision-loop` (transient)\\n- **Specialists**: `completed` | `blocked`\\n- **Auditors**: `passed` | `failed` | `blocked`\\n\"}"
